            "review_title": "Review at Nhu Lan",
            "review_text": "David M\nDoncaster East, Australia61 contributions\n0\nTucked off the main road, a Vietnamese street food mecca\nMar 2026 • Friends\nFirst time writing a review, but certainly not my first visit. I’ve been travelling to Ho Chi Minh City yearly since 2009, and I always make a point of stopping by this popular café/delicatessen/bánh mì and drinks spot.\nMy go-to is the roast ham bánh mì—you’ll see the meat cooking in a glass rotisserie, which adds to the whole experience.\nI’ll start by saying this is a busy, authentic local spot, and those looking for a more polished or “sanitary-looking” venue might initially feel hesitant. That said, I’ve never once felt unwell after eating here, and it’s always my first stop whenever I’m back.\nThe turnover is constant, so everything is fresh, and the flavours never disappoint. Honestly, it’s hard to pick a favourite—every bánh mì I’ve tried has been excellent. The fruit juices are freshly made, the food is high quality, and the prices are incredibly budget-friendly.\nA must-visit if you’re in the area.\nRead more\nInsider tip:\nDon't be hesitant. This is worth a try and good for any meal of the day.\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten March 19, 2026",
